			"Message": "chore(Maintain): Normalize shell syntax and redirect spacing across build scripts\n\nApply consistent indentation and operator placement to the Maintain directory shell utilities to align with project linting standards. Standardize redirect operators (e.g., `2> /dev/null` with space, `>/dev/null` without space where appropriate) and remove inconsistent leading tabs in `case` block bodies.\n\nKey changes:\n- **Debug/Build.sh, Run.sh, Dev-Mountain.sh, Release.sh, Release/Build.sh**: Standardize `case` statement indentation for options and profile blocks; ensure consistent spacing in `grep`, `du`, and `find` command redirections.\n- **Format.sh, Profile.sh, Save.sh**: Fix `dirname` pipeline redirections and `case` block styling.\n- **Integration/SmokeProfiles.sh**: Align `kill`, `wait`, and `grep` redirection spacing; standardize `||` operator placement for error handling.\n- **Script/* (CleanGenerated, GenerateRouteManifest, PostHogCapture, etc.)**: Unify `2> /dev/null` usage, fix `cat` and `echo` redirection spacing, and ensure `find`/`xargs` pipelines maintain consistent formatting.\n- **Test/TelemetryTreeShake.sh**: Standardize `strings` and `grep` redirections and `wc` command piping.\n\nThese changes ensure all shell scripts pass `shfmt` and `shellcheck` without warnings, improving CI reliability and code consistency.\n\nRefs #e363785695a702badc0d40679e2c77280a233e2a",
			"SHA": "0f4b5f41de621741bc76169f30dce8b811b4c248"
		},
